Cases for the use-once test dialect, shared by the two validators' tests:
`lean/FirTest/UseOnce.lean` and `crates/funk-ir/tests/use_once.rs`. Each case
starts with a line of three equals signs, `accept` or `reject`, and its name.
A case that writes a word of the use-once dialect names `toy` in its dialect
set.
The result of `toy.once` must be used exactly once in its function. Every
case holds the function `@f`, and the first op of its entry block has the
location reference `@1`, where both validators report a broken rule.

=== accept used-once-by-a-core-op
dialects toy

func @f(%n: i32) -> i32 {
^entry:
  %q: i32 = toy.once @1
  %r: i32 = add %q, %n @0
  ret %r @0
}

locs {
  @0 = unknown
  @1 = name("q")
}
=== accept used-once-by-a-toy-op
dialects toy

func @f() {
^entry:
  %q: i32 = toy.once @1
  toy.sink %q @0
  ret @0
}

locs {
  @0 = unknown
  @1 = name("q")
}
=== accept passed-once-to-a-block
dialects toy

func @f() -> i32 {
^entry:
  %q: i32 = toy.once @1
  br ^next(%q) @0
^next(%x: i32):
  ret %x @0
}

locs {
  @0 = unknown
  @1 = name("q")
}
=== accept other-values-are-free
func @f(%n: i32) -> i32 {
^entry:
  %a: i32 = add %n, %n @1
  %b: i32 = add %a, %a @0
  ret %b @0
}

locs {
  @0 = unknown
  @1 = name("a")
}
=== reject never-used
dialects toy

func @f() {
^entry:
  %q: i32 = toy.once @1
  ret @0
}

locs {
  @0 = unknown
  @1 = name("q")
}
=== reject used-twice-by-one-op
dialects toy

func @f() -> i32 {
^entry:
  %q: i32 = toy.once @1
  %r: i32 = add %q, %q @0
  ret %r @0
}

locs {
  @0 = unknown
  @1 = name("q")
}
=== reject used-by-a-toy-op-and-a-core-op
dialects toy

func @f() -> i32 {
^entry:
  %q: i32 = toy.once @1
  toy.sink %q @0
  ret %q @0
}

locs {
  @0 = unknown
  @1 = name("q")
}
=== reject passed-to-two-blocks
dialects toy

func @f(%c: i1) -> i32 {
^entry:
  %q: i32 = toy.once @1
  cond_br %c, ^a(%q), ^b(%q) @0
^a(%x: i32):
  ret %x @0
^b(%y: i32):
  ret %y @0
}

locs {
  @0 = unknown
  @1 = name("q")
}
=== reject the-second-of-two-values
dialects toy

func @f() -> i32 {
^entry:
  %p: i32 = toy.once @1
  %q: i32 = toy.once @0
  toy.sink %q @0
  toy.sink %q @0
  ret %p @0
}

locs {
  @0 = unknown
  @1 = name("q")
}
